  "name": "Question 18",
  "problem": "Calculate $\\int \\frac{10{s}^{4}}{\\sqrt{{s}^{5}+1}}\\,\\text{d}s.$",
  "worked_solution": "Let $u={s}^{5}+1.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}s}=5{s}^{4}\\,\u27f9\\,\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u={s}^{4}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nand we can solve the resulting integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{10{s}^{4}}{\\sqrt{{s}^{5}+1}}\\,\\text{d}s & =10\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{s}^{5}+1}}\\cdot {s}^{4}\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & =10\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{5}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\cdot (2\\sqrt{u})+C \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{u}+C \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{{s}^{5}+1}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
